---
// Warms the preview RUNTIME bundle (`lattice-runtime.js`) on any page that
// live-renders a slide ON LOAD — the app pages (Studio/Playground), the landing
// hero, and every component page's specimen — so the first live render's iframe
// doesn't cold-fetch it on the critical path.
//
// THE GAP THIS CLOSES. The engine bundle (`lattice-playground.js`) is warmed
// by EngineWarm / loaded directly on mount, but the runtime is a SEPARATE
// asset the parent page never fetches — it's pulled the first time a preview
// iframe writes its `srcdoc` (`<script src=runtimeUrl>`), which happens only
// AFTER the engine has loaded and the first render runs. So on a cold / hard
// refresh the two heavy fetches are SERIAL (engine, THEN runtime), and the
// runtime lands squarely on the first-render critical path — it's the bulk of
// the perf overlay's FRAME REBUILD needle even for a tiny slide (the slide
// itself parses in ~2ms; the 563KB CSS + this 137KB-gz runtime are the cost).
// See engineering/decisions/2026-07-11-preview-performance-diagnosis.md (B④,
// "warm the runtime — off the first-render critical path", previously unshipped).
//
// HOW. A `<link rel="prefetch" as="script">` appended to <head> on the page's
// `load` event (at once if the page has already loaded):
//   • it still OVERLAPS the engine load and the first render instead of waiting
//     behind them — the hero / specimen asks for the runtime only after the
//     engine (lattice-playground.js) has arrived and rendered, which is seconds
//     after `load` on a phone;
//   • it no longer starts during HTML parse. It used to be a static tag there,
//     and a 461 KB download that starts beside the fonts and the render-blocking
//     CSS counted against the page's largest paint: Lighthouse mobile, home,
//     three runs each, LCP 4.73-4.88 s -> 2.63-2.79 s, score 60-66 -> 71-78,
//     while the hero's first slide on the phone profile did not move (4.17-4.23 s
//     vs 4.06-4.15 s median, 8 loads each over HTTP/2). Record:
//     engineering/decisions/2026-10-26-lighthouse-home-runtime-prefetch.md;
//   • `prefetch` (not `preload`) keeps it at the browser's lowest priority, and,
//     because the runtime is used only inside a subframe, it also sidesteps
//     preload's "not used" console warning;
//   • the URL is the SAME content-hashed `lattice-runtime.js` the app pages'
//     `options.runtimeUrl` resolves to (both = joinBase(base, assetBase()+…)),
//     so the prefetch and the iframe's later `<script src>` share ONE cache
//     entry — a content change bumps the hash and busts both together.
//
// Non-speculative: unlike EngineWarm (which prefetches for a POSSIBLE next
// navigation and so gates on Save-Data), every app page that renders a preview
// WILL load the runtime, so there's nothing to gate — warming a definitely-used
// asset honors, not fights, a data-saving visitor's intent.
import { assetBase } from '../../playground/asset-version.mjs';
import { joinBase } from '../../lib/base-url.mjs';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const runtimeUrl = joinBase(base, assetBase() + 'lattice-runtime.js');
---

<script is:inline data-runtime-warm define:vars={{ runtimeUrl }}>
	const warm = () => {
		const link = document.createElement('link');
		link.rel = 'prefetch';
		link.as = 'script';
		link.href = runtimeUrl;
		document.head.appendChild(link);
	};
	if (document.readyState === 'complete') warm();
	else addEventListener('load', warm, { once: true });
</script>
